/tmp/whest-official-deps/whestbench/templates/dataset_card.md.j2:24:WhestBench is a benchmark for *white-box activation estimation*: given the weights of a randomly initialized ReLU multi-layer perceptron (MLP) and a strict floating-point-operation (FLOP) budget, predict the average post-activation value of every neuron when the network is fed standard Gaussian inputs.
